<!-- CONTENT -->
<div class="container subpage">
    <div class="row">
    <div class="col-sm-7">
        <div class="subpage-center">
            <div class="editarea"><h3>Fees are calculated on the NSX market capitalisation of the quoted securities using a sliding scale.</h3>
<h3>Application Fee</h3>
<p>The application fee is paid at the time the initial application for listing is made of the primary securities.  This is a once off fee.&nbsp;<strong>The application fee for ASX migrating companies is discounted to a fixed amount of $8,000 (excl GST), $2,000 for a Suitability Assessment followed by $6,000 for the lodgement of the Application. However if the company has been suspended for a long period of time then the full fees may apply.</strong></p>
<h3>Annual Fee</h3>
<p>Annual fees are payable each year.  In a full year they are calculated on a 1st July to 30 June basis.  In the first year of listing they are calculated on a pro-rata basis.  Annual fees are non-refundable.&nbsp;</p>
<h3>Additional Securities Fee&nbsp;</h3>
<p>Additional fees are required to be paid when newly issued or restricted securities are to be quoted.</p>
<h3>Notes to Fees</h3>
<h4>Minimum Share Price</h4>
<p>There is no minimum price per share for shares listed on the NSX.&nbsp; All fees are calculated as the greater of 10 cents, the initial issue price or the current market (last sale) price per share.</p>
<h4>Third Party Fees</h4>
<p>External companies to NSX charge fees for their service which are payable to those service providers, including:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Adviser Fee</strong><strong>s</strong> - External Nominated Advisers and Brokers charge a fee for their services. The amount and format of these fees is up to the issuer and Adviser to negotiate. The NSX does not become involved in these negotiations.</li>
    <li><strong>Share Registry Fees</strong> - A share registry must be appointed that is able to connect to CHESS.  Share Registries charge a fee for this service.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal Services, Audit Services and Experts Reports</strong> - Professional adviser advice may be required by the issuer.</li>
    <li><strong>CHESS Fees</strong> - Access to the ASX CS CHESS facility incurs an application and annual fee for issuers. In addition, CHESS charge other fees according to their standard schedule of fees and are billed direct to the issuer or broker.</li>
</ul>
<h3>More Information on Fees</h3>
<p>For full details of all NSX fees and charges please refer to the Listing Fees Practice Note available from the NSX website. <a href="/documents/practice_notes/PN01-ListingFees.pdf">Click here to see the Practice Note.</a></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p></div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-sm-5">
    <div class="small-table side-table">
        <div class="datagrid">
            <div class="table-responsive no-min-width"><table>
			<h3>Fee Examples (excl GST)</h3>
            <thead>  
                <tr>
                    <th>Market Capitalisation $</th>
                    <th class="algright">5 mil</th>
                    <th class="algright" >10 mil</th>
                    <th class="algright">50 mil</th>
                    <th class="algright">100 mil</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>Application<br />Fee $</th>
                    <td class="algright">40,365</td>
                    <td class="algright">59,786</td>
                    <td class="algright">95,306</td>
                    <td class="algright" >126,381</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Annual Fee $</td>
                    <td class="algright">13,947</td>
                    <td class="algright">19,691</td>
                    <td class="algright">26,176</td>
                    <td class="algright">34,282</td>
                </tr>
		        <tr>
                    <td>Additional Securities Fee $</td>
                    <td class="algright">12,663</td>
                    <td class="algright">19,796</td>
                    <td class="algright">40,795</td>
                    <td class="algright">67,045</td>
                </tr>
		        
            </tbody>
        </table></div>
